        "diagnosis": "Skill covers building deterministic D3 outputs but does not explicitly warn about SVG label elements intercepting pointer events and breaking automated click interactions. The task requires click-to-highlight linking, and the failure shows <text> intercepts pointer events so clicks never reach the circle handler/hit target.",
        "repair_instruction": "Add a section on robust interactivity for SVG marks: (1) ensure clickable elements are the topmost pointer target or set `pointer-events: none` on non-interactive overlays like labels; (2) recommend wrapping each node in a <g> with the click handler on the <g> and setting `cursor: pointer`; (3) mention Playwright-style automated tests and advise making click targets stable/accessible (e.g., add class names, data attributes, and avoid label overlap intercepting clicks). Include a minimal example snippet for bubbles with labels demonstrating `text.style('pointer-events','none')` or CSS `svg text{pointer-events:none;}`."
      }
